IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), s 47: regulations.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- The days and periods of s 47(3)(a) to (c), (4), (7), (10) and (11) are counted in tas-interpretation-time.l4; the rules below build on them.
-- A penalty is stated in penalty units; the text gives no value for a penalty unit (see NOTES.md).
-- s 47(9) is shown only as a row of dots and is not encoded.

§ `s 47(1): what regulations may prescribe`

DECLARE `Matter that regulations may prescribe` IS ONE OF
    `a matter or thing that the Act expressly or by implication empowers or directs to be prescribed`
    `a matter or thing that is necessary or convenient for giving effect to the provisions or objects of the Act`
    `forms to be used for the purposes of the Act`
    `the duties of officers or employees appointed by or under the Act, and directions for the administration of its provisions`
    `as an offence, a specified contravention of, or failure to comply with, any of the regulations`
    `some other matter`

-- src:1177 | (a) any matter or thing not inconsistent with the provisions of that Act and not repugnant to any express enactment in force, which –
-- src:1179 | (i) that Act expressly or by implication empowers or directs to be prescribed; or
-- src:1181 | (ii) is necessary or convenient for giving effect to the provisions or objects of that Act;
-- src:1183 | (b) any forms to be used for the purposes of that Act;
-- src:1185 | (c) the duties of any officers or employees appointed by or under that Act and directions for the administration of the provisions thereof;
-- src:1187 | (d) as an offence any specified contravention of, or failure to comply with, any of the regulations; and
@ref s 47(1)(a) to (d) (src:1177-1187)
GIVEN `the Act provides that the Governor or a specified authority may make regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter that regulations may prescribe`
      `it is not inconsistent with the provisions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not repugnant to any express enactment in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` `the Act provides that the Governor or a specified authority may make regulations` matter `it is not inconsistent with the provisions of the Act` `it is not repugnant to any express enactment in force` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the Act provides that the Governor or a specified authority may make regulations`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
    ELSE CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `a matter or thing that the Act expressly or by implication empowers or directs to be prescribed` THEN IF `it is not inconsistent with the provisions of the Act` AND `it is not repugnant to any express enactment in force` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording
        WHEN `a matter or thing that is necessary or convenient for giving effect to the provisions or objects of the Act` THEN IF `it is not inconsistent with the provisions of the Act` AND `it is not repugnant to any express enactment in force` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording
        WHEN `forms to be used for the purposes of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the duties of officers or employees appointed by or under the Act, and directions for the administration of its provisions` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `as an offence, a specified contravention of, or failure to comply with, any of the regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `some other matter` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1189 | (e) a penalty or a fine in respect of any such offence of an amount not exceeding such maximum as may be specified in that Act or, where no maximum amount is so specified, not exceeding 20 penalty units and, if the offence is of a continuing nature, a daily fine of such maximum amount as may be specified in that Act or, where no such maximum amount is so specified, not exceeding 5 penalty units.
@ref s 47(1)(e) penalty (src:1189)
GIVEN `the maximum penalty specified in that Act, in penalty units` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(1)(e): the most, in penalty units, the penalty for an offence under the regulations may be` `the maximum penalty specified in that Act, in penalty units` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum penalty specified in that Act, in penalty units`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN specified
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 20

-- src:1189 | (e) a penalty or a fine in respect of any such offence of an amount not exceeding such maximum as may be specified in that Act or, where no maximum amount is so specified, not exceeding 20 penalty units and, if the offence is of a continuing nature, a daily fine of such maximum amount as may be specified in that Act or, where no such maximum amount is so specified, not exceeding 5 penalty units.
@ref s 47(1)(e) daily fine (src:1189)
GIVEN `the offence is of a continuing nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum daily fine specified in that Act, in penalty units` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 47(1)(e): the most, in penalty units, the daily fine for a continuing offence under the regulations may be` `the offence is of a continuing nature` `the maximum daily fine specified in that Act, in penalty units` MEANS
    IF `the offence is of a continuing nature`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the maximum daily fine specified in that Act, in penalty units`
          WHEN JUST specified THEN JUST specified
          WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 5)
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `a matter or thing that the Act expressly or by implication empowers or directs to be prescribed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `a matter or thing that the Act expressly or by implication empowers or directs to be prescribed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `a matter or thing that the Act expressly or by implication empowers or directs to be prescribed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `a matter or thing that is necessary or convenient for giving effect to the provisions or objects of the Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `a matter or thing that is necessary or convenient for giving effect to the provisions or objects of the Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `forms to be used for the purposes of the Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `the duties of officers or employees appointed by or under the Act, and directions for the administration of its provisions` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `as an offence, a specified contravention of, or failure to comply with, any of the regulations` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1): the regulations may prescribe the matter` TRUE `some other matter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
