§ `s 47(2): forms`

-- src:1191 | (2) Where forms are prescribed by or under any Act, it shall be intended that any document in the prescribed form or to the like effect shall be a sufficient compliance with such Act, provided that any deviation therein from the prescribed form shall not be calculated to mislead or prejudice any person concerned.
@ref s 47(2) (src:1191)
GIVEN `forms are prescribed by or under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is in the prescribed form or to the like effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any deviation from the prescribed form is calculated to mislead or prejudice a person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(2): the document is a sufficient compliance with the Act` `forms are prescribed by or under an Act` `the document is in the prescribed form or to the like effect` `any deviation from the prescribed form is calculated to mislead or prejudice a person concerned` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`forms are prescribed by or under an Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the document is in the prescribed form or to the like effect`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           IF `any deviation from the prescribed form is calculated to mislead or prejudice a person concerned` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 47(2): the document is a sufficient compliance with the Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(2): the document is a sufficient compliance with the Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(2): the document is a sufficient compliance with the Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(2): the document is a sufficient compliance with the Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 47(3): publication, laying before Parliament, and taking effect`

-- src:1193 | (3) The following provisions apply to regulations made under the authority of an Act unless the authorizing Act expressly provides otherwise:
-- src:1195 | (a) if the regulations are not statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953 or are exempted from the operation of that Act, the regulations shall be published in the Gazette within 21 days after the day on which they are made;
-- src:1197 | (b) if the regulations are statutory rules within that meaning, the making of the regulations shall be notified in the Gazette within 21 days after the day on which they are made;
-- src:1199 | (c) the regulations shall be laid before each House of Parliament within the first 10 sitting days of the House after the regulations are so published or, as the case may be, the making of the regulations is so notified;
-- src:1201 | (d) the regulations shall take effect –
-- src:1203 | (i) on or from a day or date that is specified for the purpose in the regulations or that is ascertainable by reference to a period of time reckoned prospectively or retrospectively from the date of publication of the regulations in the Gazette or, as the case may be, the date of notification in the Gazette of the making of the regulations; or
-- src:1205 | (ii) if no such day or date is so specified or ascertainable, on the date of publication of the regulations in the Gazette or, as the case may be, on the date of notification in the Gazette of the making of the regulations –
-- src:1207 | but the regulations shall not be expressed to take effect on or from a day or date preceding that date of publication or notification in the Gazette where, if the regulations were so to take effect –
-- src:1209 | (iii) the rights or privileges of a person (other than the Crown in right of the State, or any department, instrumentality, authority, or agency of the State) existing at the date of that notification or publication would be prejudiced; or
-- src:1211 | (iv) liabilities or obligations would be imposed on any person (other than the Crown in right of the State, or any department, instrumentality, authority, or agency of the State) in respect of anything done or omitted to be done on or before that date of notification or publication.
@ref s 47(3) (src:1193-1211)
GIVEN `the regulations are made under the authority of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorizing Act expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(3): the provisions of paragraphs (a) to (d) apply to the regulations` `the regulations are made under the authority of an Act` `the authorizing Act expressly provides otherwise` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the regulations are made under the authority of an Act`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the authorizing Act expressly provides otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- A statutory rule that is exempted from the Rules Publication Act 1953 is taken under paragraph (a) (publication) for the reason given at s 38A(2): paragraph (a) names exempted regulations and paragraph (b) names statutory rules without exception (a fork, see NOTES.md).
-- src:1195 | (a) if the regulations are not statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953 or are exempted from the operation of that Act, the regulations shall be published in the Gazette within 21 days after the day on which they are made;
-- src:1197 | (b) if the regulations are statutory rules within that meaning, the making of the regulations shall be notified in the Gazette within 21 days after the day on which they are made;
@ref s 47(3)(a) and (b) step (src:1195-1197)
GIVEN `the regulations are statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations are exempted from the operation of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Step to be taken in the Gazette`
`s 47(3)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette for the regulations` `the regulations are statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` `the regulations are exempted from the operation of that Act` MEANS
    IF `the regulations are statutory rules within the meaning of the Rules Publication Act 1953` AND (NOT (`the regulations are exempted from the operation of that Act`))
    THEN `notification in the Gazette of the making`
    ELSE `publication in the Gazette`

-- src:1201 | (d) the regulations shall take effect –
-- src:1203 | (i) on or from a day or date that is specified for the purpose in the regulations or that is ascertainable by reference to a period of time reckoned prospectively or retrospectively from the date of publication of the regulations in the Gazette or, as the case may be, the date of notification in the Gazette of the making of the regulations; or
-- src:1205 | (ii) if no such day or date is so specified or ascertainable, on the date of publication of the regulations in the Gazette or, as the case may be, on the date of notification in the Gazette of the making of the regulations –
-- src:1207 | but the regulations shall not be expressed to take effect on or from a day or date preceding that date of publication or notification in the Gazette where, if the regulations were so to take effect –
-- src:1209 | (iii) the rights or privileges of a person (other than the Crown in right of the State, or any department, instrumentality, authority, or agency of the State) existing at the date of that notification or publication would be prejudiced; or
-- src:1211 | (iv) liabilities or obligations would be imposed on any person (other than the Crown in right of the State, or any department, instrumentality, authority, or agency of the State) in respect of anything done or omitted to be done on or before that date of notification or publication.
@ref s 47(3)(d) (src:1201-1211)
GIVEN `the day specified or ascertainable` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 47(3)(d): the day the regulations take effect` `the day specified or ascertainable` `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette` MEANS
    `s 38A(2)(d): the day an instrument other than one fixing a commencement day takes effect` `the day specified or ascertainable` `after` `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette`

-- src:1201 | (d) the regulations shall take effect –
-- src:1203 | (i) on or from a day or date that is specified for the purpose in the regulations or that is ascertainable by reference to a period of time reckoned prospectively or retrospectively from the date of publication of the regulations in the Gazette or, as the case may be, the date of notification in the Gazette of the making of the regulations; or
-- src:1205 | (ii) if no such day or date is so specified or ascertainable, on the date of publication of the regulations in the Gazette or, as the case may be, on the date of notification in the Gazette of the making of the regulations –
-- src:1207 | but the regulations shall not be expressed to take effect on or from a day or date preceding that date of publication or notification in the Gazette where, if the regulations were so to take effect –
-- src:1209 | (iii) the rights or privileges of a person (other than the Crown in right of the State, or any department, instrumentality, authority, or agency of the State) existing at the date of that notification or publication would be prejudiced; or
-- src:1211 | (iv) liabilities or obligations would be imposed on any person (other than the Crown in right of the State, or any department, instrumentality, authority, or agency of the State) in respect of anything done or omitted to be done on or before that date of notification or publication.
@ref s 47(3)(d) not before publication (src:1201-1211)
GIVEN `the day the regulations are expressed to take effect` IS A DATE
      `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the rights or privileges of a person other than the Crown existing at that date would be prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `liabilities or obligations would be imposed on a person other than the Crown in respect of anything done or omitted on or before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(3)(d): the regulations may not be expressed to take effect on a day before publication or notification` `the day the regulations are expressed to take effect` `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette` `the rights or privileges of a person other than the Crown existing at that date would be prejudiced` `liabilities or obligations would be imposed on a person other than the Crown in respect of anything done or omitted on or before that date` MEANS
    `s 38A(2)(d): an instrument may not be expressed to take effect on a day before publication or notification` `the day the regulations are expressed to take effect` `after` `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette` `with` `the rights or privileges of a person other than the Crown existing at that date would be prejudiced` `and` `liabilities or obligations would be imposed on a person other than the Crown in respect of anything done or omitted on or before that date`

#ASSERT `s 47(3): the provisions of paragraphs (a) to (d) apply to the regulations` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3): the provisions of paragraphs (a) to (d) apply to the regulations` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(3): the provisions of paragraphs (a) to (d) apply to the regulations` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette for the regulations` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `publication in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette for the regulations` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `publication in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(a) and (b): the step to be taken in the Gazette for the regulations` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `notification in the Gazette of the making`
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(d): the day the regulations take effect` (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(d): the day the regulations take effect` NOTHING (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS Date 5 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(d): the regulations may not be expressed to take effect on a day before publication or notification` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(d): the regulations may not be expressed to take effect on a day before publication or notification` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(d): the regulations may not be expressed to take effect on a day before publication or notification` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(d): the regulations may not be expressed to take effect on a day before publication or notification` (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(3)(d): the regulations may not be expressed to take effect on a day before publication or notification` (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 47(3A): regulations that are void`

-- src:1213 | (3A) Where –
-- src:1215 | (a) regulations are not published in the Gazette as required by subsection (3) (a);
-- src:1217 | (b) the making of regulations is not notified in the Gazette as required by subsection (3) (b); or
-- src:1219 | (c) regulations in relation to a matter referred to in subsection (3) (d) (iii) or (iv) are expressed to take effect on or from a day or date preceding the date of publication of those regulations in the Gazette or, as the case may be, on or from a day or date preceding the date of the notification in the Gazette of the making of those regulations –
-- src:1221 | those regulations are void.
@ref s 47(3A) (src:1213-1221)
GIVEN `the day the regulations were made` IS A DATE
      `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the regulations are expressed to take effect` IS A DATE
      `the rights or privileges of a person other than the Crown existing at that date would be prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `liabilities or obligations would be imposed on a person other than the Crown in respect of anything done or omitted on or before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(3A): the regulations are void` `the day the regulations were made` `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette` `the day the regulations are expressed to take effect` `the rights or privileges of a person other than the Crown existing at that date would be prejudiced` `liabilities or obligations would be imposed on a person other than the Crown in respect of anything done or omitted on or before that date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day of publication or notification in the Gazette`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST published THEN
        IF NOT (`s 47(3)(a) and (b): the regulations were published or notified in the Gazette within 21 days after the day they were made` `the day the regulations were made` `and` published)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE IF `s 38A(2)(d): an instrument may not be expressed to take effect on a day before publication or notification` `the day the regulations are expressed to take effect` `after` published `with` `the rights or privileges of a person other than the Crown existing at that date would be prejudiced` `and` `liabilities or obligations would be imposed on a person other than the Crown in respect of anything done or omitted on or before that date` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"

#ASSERT `s 47(3A): the regulations are void` (Date 1 2 2026) NOTHING (Date 10 2 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3A): the regulations are void` (Date 1 2 2026) (JUST (Date 22 2 2026)) (Date 22 2 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(3A): the regulations are void` (Date 1 2 2026) (JUST (Date 23 2 2026)) (Date 23 2 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3A): the regulations are void` (Date 1 2 2026) (JUST (Date 10 2 2026)) (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3A): the regulations are void` (Date 1 2 2026) (JUST (Date 10 2 2026)) (Date 5 2 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3A): the regulations are void` (Date 1 2 2026) (JUST (Date 10 2 2026)) (Date 5 2 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(3A): the regulations are void` (Date 1 2 2026) (JUST (Date 10 2 2026)) (Date 10 2 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 47(4) to (8): disallowance, and the Governor as the maker of regulations`

-- src:1223 | (4) If either House of Parliament passes a resolution, of which notice has been given within the first 15 sitting days of such House after any regulation is laid before it, that such regulation be disallowed, such regulation thereupon shall be void and thenceforth shall cease to have effect except as regards anything done thereunder prior to the passing of such resolution.
@ref s 47(4) void (src:1223)
GIVEN `the day the regulation is laid before the House` IS A DATE
      `sitting days` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day notice of the resolution was given` IS A DATE
      `the House passes a resolution that the regulation be disallowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(4): the regulation is void and ceases to have effect` `the day the regulation is laid before the House` `among` `sitting days` `notice` `the day notice of the resolution was given` `resolution` `the House passes a resolution that the regulation be disallowed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 47(4): the last of the first 15 sitting days of the House after a regulation is laid before it` `the day the regulation is laid before the House` `among` `sitting days`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        IF `the House passes a resolution that the regulation be disallowed` AND `the day notice of the resolution was given` GREATER THAN `the day the regulation is laid before the House` AND `the day notice of the resolution was given` AT MOST lastDay
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If", or notice given outside the first 15 sitting days

-- src:1223 | (4) If either House of Parliament passes a resolution, of which notice has been given within the first 15 sitting days of such House after any regulation is laid before it, that such regulation be disallowed, such regulation thereupon shall be void and thenceforth shall cease to have effect except as regards anything done thereunder prior to the passing of such resolution.
@ref s 47(4) things done (src:1223)
GIVEN `the day the thing was done under the regulation` IS A DATE
      `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(4): the thing done under the regulation is unaffected by the resolution` `the day the thing was done under the regulation` `the day the resolution was passed` MEANS
    IF `the day the thing was done under the regulation` BELOW `the day the resolution was passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- "except as regards anything done thereunder prior to the passing"

-- src:1225 | (5) Notice of the passing of every such resolution shall be gazetted forthwith by the Clerk of the House by which the same was passed.
@ref s 47(5) (src:1225)
GIVEN `a resolution under subsection (4) has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(5): the Clerk of the House by which the resolution was passed is to have notice of the passing gazetted forthwith` `a resolution under subsection (4) has been passed` MEANS
    IF `a resolution under subsection (4) has been passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Extent of a disallowance` IS ONE OF
    `only the section, division or part expressed to be disallowed`
    `the whole of the regulation`

-- src:1227 | (6) Where in any such resolution any section, division, or part of a regulation is expressed to be disallowed, the resolution shall have the effect of annulling only such section, division, or part, and in every other case such disallowance shall extend to the whole of such regulation.
@ref s 47(6) (src:1227)
GIVEN `the resolution expresses a section, division or part of the regulation to be disallowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Extent of a disallowance`
`s 47(6): the resolution annuls` `the resolution expresses a section, division or part of the regulation to be disallowed` MEANS
    IF `the resolution expresses a section, division or part of the regulation to be disallowed`
    THEN `only the section, division or part expressed to be disallowed`
    ELSE `the whole of the regulation`

-- "Made within 12 months after such disallowance" counts a regulation made on the day of the disallowance itself (a fork, see NOTES.md).
-- src:1229 | (7) Where a regulation, or any part thereof, has been disallowed as aforesaid by either House of Parliament, no regulation to the same, or substantially the same, effect made within 12 months after such disallowance shall take effect until the same has been laid upon the table of such House and 30 sitting days of such House have elapsed after the same was so laid, unless such House shall have sooner passed a resolution allowing the same.
@ref s 47(7) (src:1229)
GIVEN `the new regulation is to the same, or substantially the same, effect as the regulation or part disallowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of disallowance` IS A DATE
      `the day the new regulation was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the new regulation is laid upon the table of the House` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `sitting days` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the House has sooner passed a resolution allowing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` `the new regulation is to the same, or substantially the same, effect as the regulation or part disallowed` `the day of disallowance` `the day the new regulation was made` `the day the new regulation is laid upon the table of the House` `sitting days` `the House has sooner passed a resolution allowing it` `the day in question` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 47(7): the last day of the 12 months after the disallowance of a regulation` `the day of disallowance`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        BRANCH IF NOT (`the day the new regulation was made` AT LEAST `the day of disallowance` AND `the day the new regulation was made` AT MOST lastDay) THEN JUST FALSE   -- "within 12 months after such disallowance": the period the text fixes
               IF NOT (`the new regulation is to the same, or substantially the same, effect as the regulation or part disallowed`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
               IF `the House has sooner passed a resolution allowing it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- "unless" met
               OTHERWISE
                   CONSIDER `the day the new regulation is laid upon the table of the House`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE   -- not yet laid: "until the same has been laid"
                   WHEN JUST laid THEN
                       CONSIDER `s 47(7): the 30th sitting day of the House after the regulation is laid upon the table` laid `among` `sitting days`
                       WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE   -- the sitting days supplied do not reach the thirtieth
                       WHEN JUST thirtieth THEN IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN thirtieth THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1231 | (8) Where by any Act it is provided that regulations may be made thereunder, and the authority by whom the same are to be made is not specified, the same shall be made by the Governor.
@ref s 47(8) (src:1231)
GIVEN `an Act provides that regulations may be made under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act does not specify the authority by whom they are to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(8): the regulations are to be made by the Governor` `an Act provides that regulations may be made under it` `the Act does not specify the authority by whom they are to be made` MEANS
    IF `an Act provides that regulations may be made under it` AND `the Act does not specify the authority by whom they are to be made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"

-- The sitting days used in these tests are a fixture: the 40 consecutive days from 2 March 2026 are taken as sitting days (the real sitting days are supplied by the caller).
`fixture sitting days` MEANS LIST
    (Date 2 3 2026), (Date 3 3 2026), (Date 4 3 2026), (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 6 3 2026), (Date 7 3 2026)
  , (Date 8 3 2026), (Date 9 3 2026), (Date 10 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026), (Date 12 3 2026), (Date 13 3 2026)
  , (Date 14 3 2026), (Date 15 3 2026), (Date 16 3 2026), (Date 17 3 2026), (Date 18 3 2026), (Date 19 3 2026)
  , (Date 20 3 2026), (Date 21 3 2026), (Date 22 3 2026), (Date 23 3 2026), (Date 24 3 2026), (Date 25 3 2026)
  , (Date 26 3 2026), (Date 27 3 2026), (Date 28 3 2026), (Date 29 3 2026), (Date 30 3 2026), (Date 31 3 2026)
  , (Date 1 4 2026), (Date 2 4 2026), (Date 3 4 2026), (Date 4 4 2026), (Date 5 4 2026), (Date 6 4 2026)
  , (Date 7 4 2026), (Date 8 4 2026), (Date 9 4 2026), (Date 10 4 2026)

#ASSERT `s 47(4): the regulation is void and ceases to have effect` (Date 1 3 2026) `among` `fixture sitting days` `notice` (Date 10 3 2026) `resolution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(4): the regulation is void and ceases to have effect` (Date 1 3 2026) `among` `fixture sitting days` `notice` (Date 10 3 2026) `resolution` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(4): the regulation is void and ceases to have effect` (Date 1 3 2026) `among` `fixture sitting days` `notice` (Date 1 3 2026) `resolution` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(4): the regulation is void and ceases to have effect` (Date 1 3 2026) `among` `fixture sitting days` `notice` (Date 15 4 2026) `resolution` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(4): the thing done under the regulation is unaffected by the resolution` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(4): the thing done under the regulation is unaffected by the resolution` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(5): the Clerk of the House by which the resolution was passed is to have notice of the passing gazetted forthwith` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(5): the Clerk of the House by which the resolution was passed is to have notice of the passing gazetted forthwith` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(6): the resolution annuls` TRUE EQUALS `only the section, division or part expressed to be disallowed`
#ASSERT `s 47(6): the resolution annuls` FALSE EQUALS `the whole of the regulation`
#ASSERT `s 47(8): the regulations are to be made by the Governor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(8): the regulations are to be made by the Governor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(8): the regulations are to be made by the Governor` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 47(7): disallowance on 1 March 2026; the 12 months end on 1 March 2027; a regulation laid on 3 March 2026 has its 30th following sitting day on 2 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 3 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) `fixture sitting days` TRUE (Date 4 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 3 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 5 4 2026)) `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 3 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2027) (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2027) (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(7): the new regulation may not take effect on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) `fixture sitting days` FALSE (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 47(10) to (12): filing and recording`

-- src:1235 | (10) Every regulation made after the passing of this Act and before the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996 shall be filed and recorded in the office of the Attorney-General, but no regulation shall be challenged, or the validity thereof impugned, on the ground of the non-observance of this provision, nor shall it be necessary to prove compliance therewith in any proceedings under or in relation to such regulation.
@ref s 47(10) (src:1235)
GIVEN `the regulation was made after the passing of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation was made before the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(10): the regulation is to be filed and recorded in the office of the Attorney-General` `the regulation was made after the passing of the Act` `the regulation was made before the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` MEANS
    IF `the regulation was made after the passing of the Act` AND `the regulation was made before the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- "after the passing of this Act and before the commencement": the period the text fixes

-- src:1235 | (10) Every regulation made after the passing of this Act and before the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996 shall be filed and recorded in the office of the Attorney-General, but no regulation shall be challenged, or the validity thereof impugned, on the ground of the non-observance of this provision, nor shall it be necessary to prove compliance therewith in any proceedings under or in relation to such regulation.
@ref s 47(10) no challenge (src:1235)
GIVEN `the ground of the challenge is non-observance of the filing and recording` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(10): the regulation may not be challenged on the ground of non-observance of the filing and recording` `the ground of the challenge is non-observance of the filing and recording` MEANS
    IF `the ground of the challenge is non-observance of the filing and recording` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- src:1235 | (10) Every regulation made after the passing of this Act and before the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996 shall be filed and recorded in the office of the Attorney-General, but no regulation shall be challenged, or the validity thereof impugned, on the ground of the non-observance of this provision, nor shall it be necessary to prove compliance therewith in any proceedings under or in relation to such regulation.
@ref s 47(10) no proof (src:1235)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under or in relation to the regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(10): it is not necessary to prove compliance with the filing and recording in proceedings under or in relation to the regulation` `the proceedings are under or in relation to the regulation` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are under or in relation to the regulation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- src:1237 | (11) Every regulation made on or after the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996 is to be filed and recorded by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel in the responsible Department in relation to the Legislation Publication Act 1996.
@ref s 47(11) (src:1237)
GIVEN `the regulation was made on or after the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(11): the regulation is to be filed and recorded by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel in the responsible Department in relation to the Legislation Publication Act 1996` `the regulation was made on or after the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` MEANS
    IF `the regulation was made on or after the commencement of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- "on or after the commencement": the period the text fixes

-- src:1239 | (12) A regulation may not be challenged, or its validity may not be impugned, on the ground of the non-observance of subsection (11) and it is not necessary to prove compliance with that subsection in any proceedings under or in relation to that regulation.
@ref s 47(12) (src:1239)
GIVEN `the ground of the challenge is non-observance of subsection (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(12): the regulation may not be challenged on the ground of non-observance of subsection (11)` `the ground of the challenge is non-observance of subsection (11)` MEANS
    IF `the ground of the challenge is non-observance of subsection (11)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- src:1239 | (12) A regulation may not be challenged, or its validity may not be impugned, on the ground of the non-observance of subsection (11) and it is not necessary to prove compliance with that subsection in any proceedings under or in relation to that regulation.
@ref s 47(12) no proof (src:1239)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under or in relation to the regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(12): it is not necessary to prove compliance with subsection (11) in proceedings under or in relation to the regulation` `the proceedings are under or in relation to the regulation` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are under or in relation to the regulation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"


#ASSERT `s 47(10): the regulation is to be filed and recorded in the office of the Attorney-General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(10): the regulation is to be filed and recorded in the office of the Attorney-General` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(10): the regulation is to be filed and recorded in the office of the Attorney-General` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
